Academic Context

This project was developed as part of:

TravelStack: Microservices-Based Travel Package Booking System

The objective was to design and develop a structured digital travel platform that enables users to explore travel packages, check availability, make bookings, complete payments, and manage their travel reservations efficiently.

Problem Statement

Traditional travel booking processes often face several operational challenges:

Lack of a centralized platform for travel package management

Difficulty checking real-time package availability

Manual or disconnected booking and payment processes

Limited integration between booking, payment, and package management

Difficulty maintaining accurate booking and payment records

This leads to:

Delayed booking confirmations

Inconsistent availability information

Payment and booking coordination issues

Poor data organization

Increased administrative workload

There is a clear need for a secure, scalable, and integrated digital travel platform that streamlines package discovery, booking, payment processing, and availability management through a microservices architecture.

Survey Conducted & Common Issues Addressed

A survey of 22 respondents was conducted to understand travel habits, booking preferences, and package selection factors. The results showed that users mainly consider price, transportation, activities, and accommodation when choosing a package. The survey also highlighted the need for easy booking, centralized information, and real-time package availability.

TravelStack addresses these issues by providing a centralized platform for package browsing, availability checking, booking, and payment.

Empathy Map – TravelStack

Thinks & Feels: Users want travel booking to be simple, secure, affordable, and reliable.

